      "type": "action",
      "img": "icons/commodities/materials/feather-orange.webp",
      "system": {
        "active": true,
        "description": "<p>The rust monster targets one nonmagical metal object—armor or a weapon—worn or carried by a creature within 5 feet of itself.</p><p><em>Dexterity Saving Throw:</em> DC , the creature with the object.</p><p><em>Failure:</em> The object takes a -1 penalty to the AC it offers (armor) or to its attack rolls (weapon). Armor is destroyed if the penalty reduces its AC to 10, and a weapon is destroyed if its penalty reaches -5. The penalty can be removed by casting the <em>Mending</em> spell on the armor or weapon.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-4QbvfWBnYI6ImcGC\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>This feature also provides a <strong>Damaged</strong> Enchantment effect that will modify the targeted object. Due to the fact that the equipment penalty can be applied multiple times, the enchantment needs to be dragged from this item's Effects tab onto the target Item's sheet.</p></section>",
        "definition": {
          "schemaVersion": 1,
          "id": "action:srd-antennae",
